  "reasoning": "The claim was denied with CO-97 (bundling), which is a medical policy denial rather than a data or information error, so resubmission or providing records is not the correct next step. Since the payer offers peer-to-peer review and a denial is on the table, requesting a P2P is a valid, low-cost action to challenge the bundling determination before escalating to a formal appeal. The patient has no financial responsibility (0% coinsurance, $0 deductible), so billing the patient is inappropriate.",
